  "breakdowns": [],
  "method": "Each year's official ranking PDF (parkserve.tpl.org/downloads/historic/<year>_ParkScoreRank.pdf) is read by word position; for each city row the script takes the rank and the total score out of 100. For 2012-2017 the score is the column just before the park-bench rating; from 2018 on it is the last number before the repeated city name. NYC's rank by year is in rank_series.",
  "caveats": [
    "Index years are the years TPL published the rankings; the 2026 index is built mostly from data gathered in 2025.",
    "TPL changed the scoring several times (scores through 2017 were published alongside a park-bench rating, the system was overhauled in 2019 and an equity component was added in 2020), and the number of cities ranked grew from 40 in 2012 to about 100, so scores and ranks are not strictly comparable across years.",
    "New York ranked 20 in 2026.",
    "In the 2026 PDF the row ranked 95 is labeled Louisville-Jefferson County at the left and Las Vegas at the right; its figures match Louisville's 2025 row, so it is read as Louisville and Las Vegas is left out of the peers."
  ],
